{"shortDescription":"By Avinash  P and Ragini MathurLatin American currencies and stocks were mixed on Monday as a softer U.S. dollar offered some support, while military escalations in the Middle East drove oil prices and global bond yields higher, renewing global inflation concerns.MSCI's Latin American currency inde…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Avinash  P and Ragini Mathur"]},{"type":"p","children":["Latin American currencies and stocks were mixed on Monday as a softer U.S. dollar offered some support, while military escalations in the Middle East drove oil prices and global bond yields higher, renewing global inflation concerns."]},{"type":"p","children":["MSCI's Latin American currency index (.MILA00000CUS) rose 0.2%, remaining on track for a subdued monthly performance."]},{"type":"p","children":["Support from a broadly softer U.S. dollar through August was offset by the region's underperformance against AI-driven emerging-market peers and renewed geopolitical uncertainty."]},{"type":"p","children":["On Monday, the dollar index ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TVC:DXY","text":"TVC:DXY"}},", which tracks the greenback against six major currencies, eased 0.2% as traders awaited key U.S. jobs data later this week ahead of the Federal Reserve's September policy decision."]},{"type":"p","children":["The dollar has regained some ground late last week after expectations of a September Fed rate hike increased. Fed Chair Kevin Warsh said on Friday that policymakers would \"have work to do\" if inflation failed to return to the central bank's 2% target, signaling that further tightening could be needed."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Our base case remains that steady progress in underlying inflation will allow the Fed to keep rates unchanged this year,\" said UBS analysts in a note."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Although the risk of a September hike has increased, the latest sequential inflation data remain consistent with further disinflation.\""]},{"type":"p","children":["Oil prices rose more than 2% after the U.S. attacked an Iranian island in the Strait of Hormuz and Tehran said it had retaliated."]},{"type":"p","children":["The rally supported assets in the region's oil-producing economies but also pushed global bond yields higher, reviving inflation concerns."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Latin American stock index (.MILA00000PUS) added 0.7%, but was still headed for monthly losses."]},{"type":"p","children":["In ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.reuters.com/world/brazil/","linkText":"Brazil"}},", equities ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}," jumped 1% and were on track to clock in their ninth straight day of gains, with oil giant Petrobras ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:PETR3","text":"BMFBOVESPA:PETR3"}}," the biggest boost on the benchmark index, up 3%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Central bank data showed the nation's gross debt as a share of gross domestic product rose to 82.5% in July from 81.9% a month earlier."]},{"type":"p","children":["Against this backdrop, Brazilian Vice President Geraldo Alckmin said the country has room both to restrain public spending and accelerate economic growth, arguing that such a combination would help reduce the debt-to-GDP ratio."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"The significant rise in public debt continues to stand out,\" XP economist Tiago Sbardelotto said, noting that gross debt reached its highest level since April 2021 while net debt hit a record high."]},{"type":"p","children":["The country's Finance Minister Dario Durigan said that some social programs could eventually cease to be mandatory expenditures, a move he said would give policymakers greater flexibility in managing the federal budget."]},{"type":"p","children":["The real ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDBRL","text":"FX_IDC:USDBRL"}}," rose 0.2%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Colombia's peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCOP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCOP"}}," extended Friday's sharp decline after the country's budget bill pointed to a much wider-than-expected deficit for 2026 and 2027. The currency was on track for its worst month since July 2025, while Bogota stocks ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BVC:ICAP","text":"BVC:ICAP"}}," rose 0.9%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Chile's peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCLP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCLP"}}," weakened 0.5%, while the country's stock benchmark ","BCS:SP_IPSA"," fell 1.1% after data showed copper output dropped 9.4% year-on-year in July, hit by severe storms in mining regions."]},{"type":"p","children":["Argentina's Merval index ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BCBA:IMV","text":"BCBA:IMV"}}," rose 2.5%, but remained on track for its steepest monthly decline since February."]},{"type":"p","children":["Key Latin American stock indexes and currencies at 1904 GMT:"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Stock indexes"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Latest"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Daily % change"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["MSCI Emerging Markets ","CBOE:EFS"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["1720.12"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["-0.12"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["MSCI LatAm (.MILA00000PUS)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3052.63"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["0.72"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Brazil Bovespa ",